    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d535">

                <pb facs="0650" n="1484" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1484"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 656.119/432</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Netherland Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">De
                            Beaufort</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-05-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 4, 1918</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to accept the recent
                    proposition of the United States Government concerning the three ships which
                    will leave [for] the Netherlands loaded with grain.</p>
                <p>This proposition is understood by my Government as follows:</p>
                <p>The Netherland ships <hi rendition="#italic">Java, Stella</hi> and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hollandia</hi> will leave for the Netherlands loaded
                    with grain, upon three ships of equivalent tonnage leaving the Netherlands, of
                    which two will proceed to United States ports and one to Buenos Aires. The three
                    last-mentioned ships will upon their arrival be enabled to load grain of the
                    amount which has been placed at the disposal of the Netherland Government and
                    they will receive all the facilities for their return to the Netherlands upon
                    the <hi rendition="#italic">Java, Stella</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hollandia</hi> or equivalent tonnage returning from the Netherlands.</p>
                <p>Please accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. de Beaufort</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
